Well.... how about making it accesible only to those who've advanced
beyond basic in "flail"? Just thinking that perhaps if flail is the
"close" analog of wielding a rooster-lizard by the tail, it'd still be
unweildly for those only basically familiar with the mechanics, but
someone who's skilled (or perhaps expert) might reasonably be expected
to manage it.

So now it's two skill slots. And it would make a formerly
uninteresting weapon skill worth cultivating for the characters who
can advance to skilled in flail -- and it makes the possibility off
limits for (nearly) all of the combat wombats (except the Samurai).
Which turns it turns a former no-brainer (why use a flail?) into a
more considered choice for some classes... especially for classes like
the priest and the caveman for whom a lot of weapons (all edged
weapons?) are off limits.

(Also might be interesting to give that to-hit-with-chicken bonus to
monsters who use flails frequently, like the sergeant.)

In any case, it's definitely interesting to have the whole rubber
chicken thing revisited.



